    "performance": "Throughput and benchmark values are Groq-advertised observations, not independent Build Loop benchmarks or end-to-end latency SLAs.",
    "rate_limits": "Reference limits below are the Developer-plan values displayed on the models page at capture time. Limits apply at organization level, can vary by account, and must be confirmed in the Groq console.",
    "pricing": "List prices are snapshots, exclude applicable server-side tool charges, and must be reverified before billing decisions.",
    "preview": "Preview models are not recommended for production and may change or disappear on short notice.",
    "retired": "lifecycle 'retired' means the announced shutdown date has passed and the model no longer appears on the models page, the rate-limits page, or the runtime models endpoint. Enterprise committed-spend contracts may still be served where the deprecation notice carved them out. Technical fields on a retired entry carry values_as_of and are last-known values for migration reference, not current offerings.",
    "active_models_api": "GET https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/models was queried on 2026-08-18 with a Developer-plan key and returned 13 active IDs. Neither llama-3.1-8b-instant nor llama-3.3-70b-versatile was present, confirming the 2026-08-16 shutdown. minimaxai/minimax-m2.7 was also absent, which is expected for a non-Enterprise key and is not evidence of removal. Runtime pricing and context values for the 12 documented IDs matched the models page exactly.",
    "undocumented_runtime_models": "The 2026-08-18 runtime listing also returned allam-2-7b (owner SDAIA, 4,096 context, json_object mode only, no pricing block). No page under console.groq.com/docs describes it, so its lifecycle, pricing, and support status cannot be established from primary documentation. It is deliberately excluded from models[] rather than recorded on runtime evidence alone.",
    "stale_capability_pages": "The tool-use page still lists llama-3.3-70b-versatile and llama-3.1-8b-instant in its capability matrix after their shutdown. source_precedence resolves this: the deprecations page outranks capability-specific pages."
  },
